                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2cbcc220-a395-4911-a180-eca57e99e9b8",
                                                "sense_id": "c8c8f0be-1247-3862-b731-c86c4f2e13f8",
                                                "text": "\"In the old days, heaps of unmarried women were companions, and let me tell you, my dear girl, they had a much better time than they have now, with all this jazzing and short skirts and pretending to have careers. The modern girl hasn't a scrap of decent feeling or sentiment about her. Money--money and notoriety, that's all she's after. That's what we fought the war for--and that's what we've come back to!\" \"George, do keep to the point. Miss Dorland doesn't jazz--\""
                                            },
